  "notes": "Form 1040 Line 16 v2 (ADR-0038 D2): the QDCG Worksheet as the single declared rule-artifact.v3 successor to v1. A conditional_dependency_set node (ADR-0037) gates on qualified dividends > 0 and the two declared-absence capital-gain fact types, placed first and unconditionally in the outer `all` so its own false-condition contract - not incidental operand order - grounds the qualified-zero reduction to the unchanged ordinary-bracket result (the confirmed Repair 2 shape, docs/prototypes/qdcg-worksheet/repair2/design.md). When qualified dividends are positive, an absent declaration produces one non-publication walk naming every currently-absent declaration; both declarations present and 'no' publishes the worksheet result (preferential-base binding on qualified dividends, ordinary-portion subtraction, rate-slice comparison via a dedicated flat preferential bracket table, final minimum against the unmodified ordinary-bracket result on total taxable income); either declaration 'yes' yields the committed inapplicable/guard_inapplicable disposition, structurally distinct from the absence path. Expressed entirely in the closed committed expression vocabulary (choose/compare/subtract/max/bracket_fold/round, plus add/categorical_compare/category_literal/ref already in the vocabulary) - no new evaluator operation. v1 remains historical."
